            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "=You are a support ticket triage system. Analyze the incoming support request and \nreturn a JSON object with these exact fields. No prose, no markdown — only valid JSON.\n\nSchema:\n{\n  \"category\": \"billing\" | \"technical\" | \"feature_request\" | \"complaint\" | \"onboarding\" | \"other\",\n  \"confidence\": < float 0.0 - 1.0,\n  \"urgency\":  \"critical\" | \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\",\n  \"sentiment\": \"frustrated\" | \"neutral\" | \"positive\",\n  \"summary\": \"<one sentence, max 20 words>\",\n  \"draft_response\": \"<professional, empathetic first-response email to the customer, 3-5 sentences>\",\n  \"internal_notes\": \"<bullet points for the agent: what to check, what was implied, any red flags>\"\n}\nConfidence:\n- your certainty about the category and urgency\n\nUrgency rules:\n- critical: service down, data loss, security issue, explicit churn threat\n- high: blocking workflow, no workaround found\n- medium: non-blocking, workaround exists\n- low: general question, feature request, positive feedback"
            },
            {
              "content": "=From.Name: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.name }}\nFrom.Email: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.email }}\nSubject: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.subject }}\nBody: \n{{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.Body }}"
            }
          ]
        },
